00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:30.790
So yesterday we went
through quantum mechanics

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:38.110
and discussed the solutions
of the Schrodinger equation.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:42.190
We started with the
one-dimensional problem

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.140
is the quantum well.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.430
Two-dimensional problem-- now
we call them a quantum wire.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:54.430
And then, say you can
extend that to a 3D--

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:55.850
that's easy.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.030
And then I gave a
harmonic wave solution

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.950
for the harmonic oscillator.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.150
I gave you the result. But I
said I have my way to solve it.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.230
And then I don't have a way
to solve rigid rotor my way.

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:12.520
Maybe you can find it.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:16.420
And the electron-- we
give the results, right?

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:19.960
And, in fact, I said that
you can also do the electron.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.720
And I know that you
can do it and find out.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.560
So for different
problems, the difference

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.430
is really the potential in
the Schrodinger equation

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:33.880
plus a boundary condition
that [INAUDIBLE] determine

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.850
why some of the solution,
like quantum well,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.520
the energy level is a
proportion of n square,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.880
the harmonic oscillator
is the proportion of u n,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.300
and the electrons u
atoms is 1 over n square.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:50.410
Those are because of the
constraint of different shapes

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.930
of the potentials.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:57.670
And then why we discussed
1D and 2D problems?

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:00.850
The important
message that we get

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.000
is, if it's a 1
degree of freedom,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.889
one-dimensional problem,
we have one quantum number.

00:02:08.889 --> 00:02:12.670
And two-dimensional problem,
we'll have to quantum numbers.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.700
And three-dimensional
problem, like atoms,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.520
we have three quantum numbers.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.320
And, of course, later
on we add the spin

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:27.250
because that's not something
you can get from the Schrodinger

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.960
equation.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:34.570
And then, quantum
state is each set

00:02:34.570 --> 00:02:36.310
of [INAUDIBLE]
unique combinations

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:41.090
of those quantum numbers
give you one quantum state.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:45.040
The problem is sometimes
different quantum states

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.180
have the same energy.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.380
So when we can, we
say-- when states

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.510
have same-- different
states have same energy,

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.610
those states are degenerate.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:59.710
And we can count the
degeneracy of those states.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:03.940
And those are later on
important because, essentially,

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:05.260
when we do--

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.850
they count the
number of particles--

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:10.180
like we did in first
chapter, first two lectures--

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.170
we need counting.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.480
We need to do the
counting correctly.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:17.500
So degeneracy is later
on going to be evolved

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:21.880
into a density of states.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.790
And spin is something
we cannot easily--

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.530
we cannot get from
Schrodinger equation.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.710
I have to go to relativistic.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.560
And-- but the--

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:41.080
for electrons, it's a 1/2
spin, positive minus 1/2 half.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.000
And those are fermions.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:47.650
And photons, pholons,
are molecules

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:50.770
that are uncharged bosons.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:57.160
And for fermions, the
Pauli Exclusion Principle

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:03.740
says each quantum state can
have maximum of one particle.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.660
So if it's a fermion
particle, each quantum state

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.430
can only have one
to the maximum.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:15.580
You [INAUDIBLE] So
that's easy to count.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.190
And for boson,
each quantum state

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.329
can have an infinite number.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:25.900
So this is-- when you think
about this harmonic oscillator,

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.480
the energy is n times h bar.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:33.310
And h bar mu--
actually, h bar omega--

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.190
the n could be 0, 1, 2, 3.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:41.890
Those [INAUDIBLE] many
[INAUDIBLE] n numbers.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:46.280
So this is what we talked about.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:55.810
And in those examples, the
wave function are confined.

00:04:55.810 --> 00:05:01.210
When I have a quantum
well or quantum wire,

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:05.230
the wave function is in this
space that I'm discussing.

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.810
When I have an atom,
the wave function

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.770
is limited to
surrounding the nuclei.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.190
So, oscillator--
that's the local.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:19.760
So this is what we
discussed so far.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.610
And today, where I'm going is--

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.240
I'm going to put
the atoms together

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.760
to have solid crystals.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.690
And how-- this
putting them together,

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:41.660
how they will change the energy
states in what we discussed?

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:48.850
So what are we going
to discuss today

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:51.235
is the energy levels in solids.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.760
Particularly, I'll
focus on electron today.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.900
And, hopefully, by the
end of the lecture,

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:17.570
you will appreciate
why we have metals.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.040
We have semiconductors.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.200
We have insulators.

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:23.510
These are all daily encounters.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:27.260
But until you have
this quantum picture,

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:29.780
you really can't explain.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:47.140
And so we have metals,
semiconductors, and insulators.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:53.920
And one very useful mathematical
theorem that I introduced today

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:58.510
is the so-called Bloch Theorem.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:09.820
It's a-- this is a
theorem that applies when

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.130
the potential is a periodic.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:15.160
So when I deal with
crystals, the atoms

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.830
are arranged in
periodic fashion.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.740
And because of
this periodicity, I

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:24.160
can solve the problem even
though the crystal is--

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:29.540
an ideal crystal is an infinite
periodic arrangement of atoms.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.310
And because of periodicity,
I can fold all the problems

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.110
into one period.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:37.900
And that's very beautiful.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:40.840
And, in fact, the
Bloch Theorem is

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:45.220
valid for all waves,
all periodic structure

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:48.170
when you have wave
[INAUDIBLE] inside.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:53.350
And when you deal with the
heat conduction equation,

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.030
or when you deal
with the transport--

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.680
when there is a
temperature gradient,

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:00.520
this is no longer
valid or diffusion.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.860
And for several years
I've been trying

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:08.450
to say, what's a corresponding
CRM in the diffusion regime?

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.000
And because when
I do a composite

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:17.000
and those kind of problems,
transport problems--

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.215
a composite that has many,
many different materials--

00:08:20.215 --> 00:08:23.390
[INAUDIBLE] think about two,
an A and a B. My simplest is--

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:24.320
I take a [INAUDIBLE].

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.680
Can I solve that
[INAUDIBLE] problem

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.950
and yet to be representative
that I'm dealing

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.720
with the whole structure?

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:37.470
So those are the things that
are a good question to ask.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:42.490
And so let's start.

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:46.720
We say-- we're dealing
with electrons.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.020
And in the last
lecture, yesterday,

00:08:50.020 --> 00:08:52.720
we deal with the
electron when we say

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.170
our model is, I have an atom.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:09:00.850
And I have electron.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:05.320
If you'll recall, at the end
we show the wave functions.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:09.160
We showed and computed
the different n equals 1.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.350
Say, for example,
the wave function

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:16.340
with three quantum number,
1, 0, 0, and, of course,

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.280
electron spin--

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:19.840
that's an increase of 1.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:20.730
[INAUDIBLE] equals 0.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:22.640
M equals 0.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.740
The [INAUDIBLE] functions
is the lowest energy level,

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.980
spherical wave function
that [INAUDIBLE]

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:38.520
And so this is, of course, you
can have higher-- other wave

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.200
functions and combinations.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.815
And now, my question is,
what about this is a simple--

00:09:46.815 --> 00:09:48.960
you think about hydrogen atom.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:52.900
What happens to
hydrogen molecule

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.880
when I put two atoms
close together?

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:02.530
So in the case of
single atom, I have--

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:09.700
this n equals 1 energy
level and n equals 2.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.540
In the hydrogen model,
we have the energy

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:19.780
is degenerate is minus 13.6
electron volts over n square.

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:27.920
36-- 13.6 electron volts is
also another energy unit.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.396
Sometimes people use it
[INAUDIBLE] 1 [INAUDIBLE]..

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:39.160
And-- so this is, of
course, we say degenerate

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:42.070
because I have three
quantum lumber,

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:47.500
n l m and plus the
spin quantum number.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.940
So if I have one hydrogen
atom-- let's say atom,

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:56.810
the electron sits in
the lowest energy level.

00:10:56.810 --> 00:11:00.120
And now, if I put
2 hydrogen atoms--

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:02.240
so I have 1 hydrogen atom.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.360
Those are the electron
wave function.

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:06.830
If you recall, it's a spherical.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.980
And I have another-- so
this is 1 hydrogen atom.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:18.560
And I have another
hydrogen atom and electron

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.320
is spherical wave function.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:29.700
Now, when they interact with
each other to form a molecule,

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:34.420
the electron wave
function start to overlap.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.170
And the Pauli Exclusion
Principle could come in.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.700
You can't do that.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.410
Now, the two electron--

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:43.990
each hydrogen has one electron.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:49.610
The two electron cannot
have the same wave function

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.910
because of the Pauli Exclusion.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:56.220
And one quantum state
doesn't take two electrons.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.810
So what happens?

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:03.370
And they will have to
modify their quantum state

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.350
and split it.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.450
And then the
splitting gives you--

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:12.040
if you go to solve
the wave function,

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.460
you'll say, OK,
this is the atom--

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.180
hydrogen atom.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:23.350
In one case, it's wave
function is more each one

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.670
separated from each other.

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:26.595
And the other case--

00:12:26.595 --> 00:12:28.930
this wave function
is the probability

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:33.520
of finding electrons, remember,
if you do complex conjugate.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.670
And the other case, you
have the wave function more

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.930
surrounding them.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:42.000
This is a sigma bond.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:49.900
Covalent bonding-- and
that's the strongest,

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:52.020
the lower energy.

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:58.690
This is the anti-bond,
sigma star higher energy.

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:00.720
So what happens is
that this energy--

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.510
the single energy
of our atom now--

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.180
because of Pauli
Exclusion Principle,

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:11.700
when they have two electrons
for the identical states,

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:12.700
they can't do it.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.500
So they split into two small--

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:21.090
with separation of
the two energy levels.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:23.730
So the states split
into from one to two.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:32.280
So this is the
higher energy level.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.370
This is lower energy level.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:41.090
Now with this, I can
ask the question,

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:45.550
what if I put the hydrogen
atom into a chain, not just

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.360
a molecule?

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.880
And if I have any--

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:58.280
N hydrogen atom,
what's going to happen?

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:01.250
They are capital N,
not like this small n.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:03.170
If I have capital
N atoms, what's

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.820
going to happen to increase one?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.302
AUDIENCE: The molecules
[INAUDIBLE] keep splitting?

00:14:08.302 --> 00:14:09.010
PROFESSOR: Right.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.675
It's split into N energy levels.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.930
And, similarly, n equals 2--

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.590
so basically if I have--

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:24.310
you will have energy split
into each of this [INAUDIBLE]

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:28.320
are split into energy level.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:31.020
And, now, of course,
that depends on here

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.150
is, how large is this spread?

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.580
And this too could
actually overlap.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:40.290
This is originally 13.6
eV divided by n square.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:42.750
So this is a few eV.

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:45.375
If this split didn't start
to overlap with each other,

00:14:45.375 --> 00:14:48.630
you have almost a continuous.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:51.450
Those are relatively
small level of separation

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.150
between energy levels.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:59.430
So this gives us a
precursor to what

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:07.650
happens if I have a
one-dimensional atomic chain.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:13.170
So-- crystals--
let's take it bigger.

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:19.455
So my simplest picture is a
one-dimensional arrangement

00:15:19.455 --> 00:15:23.080
of crystals are the periodic
arrangement of atoms.

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.535
So I have periodic
arrangement of atoms.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.690
And the potential is a periodic.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:39.020
So around each
atom, the electron--

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:46.190
recall, the quantum potential
is negative [INAUDIBLE] over R.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:49.740
So, here in the--
when I close to atom,

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.230
the potential is lowest.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.270
And in between is
the higher potential.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:59.150
So I have periodical
potential field to the charge.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:05.510
So now we want to find out--

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:08.880
we already got some idea this
is what's going to happen.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.660
The energy is going to split.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:16.305
And we want to find the
splitted energy levels.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:24.840
And we're going to solve the
Schrodinger equation for that.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:27.110
And, in fact, that there are--

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:33.950
really, this problem, you can
look at it from three pictures.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:35.670
Let me explain briefly.

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:38.090
The first picture I read, it
said the atomic [INAUDIBLE]

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:40.040
overlapping.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.850
So if I draw-- if I
simplify this potential,

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:48.500
I get a square rather
than what I draw 1 over R.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:51.265
So here I have [INAUDIBLE]--

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:59.980
So this is a
[INAUDIBLE] periodic.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:12.609
That's another way I
model those potential.

00:17:12.609 --> 00:17:14.740
The real atoms is never--

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:15.880
just so this is square.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:19.630
It's-- like I say, this
is very much depend on--

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:24.250
the energy level depends
on the potential shape.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:26.980
And, of course,
if I do a square,

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:28.540
then I have the picture.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:31.510
I have quantum wells.

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:36.640
If it's an infinite potential,
I have this standing wave

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:39.970
for electrons quantum wells.

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:44.200
And-- but say this is a
normally not an infinite.

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.470
They are certain height.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:50.590
So it turns out from wave
mechanics perspective--

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:53.440
later on, when we
do chapter 5, you'll

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:57.170
see the wave can tunnel
from one side to the other.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.080
So they start
[INAUDIBLE] overlapping.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:02.300
And then the quantum mechanic
Pauli Explosion Principle

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:06.520
say you can't overlap
the quantum state.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.710
So they will split at this--

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:13.630
this will split into, again,
the ones that we described here,

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:17.740
when atom of those
start to overlap.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.300
And these are the ones--

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:21.190
this is a one
picture, I say, OK, we

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.460
start thinking about the
quantum well picture.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.295
And the other picture is, I
have a free electron moving

00:18:28.295 --> 00:18:28.795
in space.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:37.478
And when free electron moving in
space and when they start to--

00:18:37.478 --> 00:18:39.520
so those are the electron
with the higher energy.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:42.510
They start to see
a bump potential

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:47.750
underneath it, a periodic
bump potential underneath it.

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:51.590
And, in that case,
what happened is if--

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:54.020
some of you may
have the experience

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.680
using the interference filter in
your lab-- optical interference

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.690
filters in your lab.

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:02.570
So that's an optical
wave comes in.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:06.740
And the interference filter,
is a typically periodical layer

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:10.380
deposition with different
refractive index.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.960
So what happens is,
then, some of the wave

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.920
will transmit through,
others reflect back.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:18.275
That's why I say you
can get lateral lines

00:19:18.275 --> 00:19:20.810
in the interference filter.

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:27.230
So the reflected back ones are
the ones that do not exist.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:29.460
Those are the ones--
the wave cannot exist.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:32.700
So this is the gap
here in the solid.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:37.370
This is a-- what this leads to
is a semiconductor with a band

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:40.280
gap.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:43.040
So you have this two picture.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:46.670
And the third picture is what
I'm going to actually solve.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.950
I solve the
Schrodinger equation--

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:53.040
another solution tells us
without the energy level.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:57.850
And all this will converge
into what we said already.

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:07.170
So, here I have the this
is the periodicity T.

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.230
And let's say under
my picture here,

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:14.460
I'm going to take a
one-unit cell, one period,

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.140
and trying to solve
the Schrodinger

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:19.230
equation in that period.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.570
I can take any period.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.620
So I put my coordinate--

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:27.580
here is my origin
of the coordinate.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.320
And this is 0.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.640
And this is the x direction.

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:33.395
And here is a.

00:20:33.395 --> 00:20:36.370
And here is-- let's
say-- because this

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:38.402
is on the other side--
this is a minus b.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.880
And from minus b to a,
that's an-- add together

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:49.540
is my period T.

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:53.260
And I want to solve this
Schrodinger equation

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.610
in this one period.

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:59.230
But I want to represent the
whole structure as a periodic.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:05.410
My potential is repeating
from every minus b to a.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:07.690
So here, the potential
is at the bottom.

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:09.550
Let's say the potential is 0.

00:21:09.550 --> 00:21:11.395
Here the potential is u0.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:20.770
So for an electron in one
region is 0 potential.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:24.630
The other region
is a u0 potential.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:27.870
And now I want to say, what
are the allowable energy

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:32.572
levels of this electron in
such a periodic potential?

00:21:32.572 --> 00:21:33.405
This is my question.

00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:41.210
So I will have to write
down the Schrodinger

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:42.680
equation for each region.

00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:45.770
Between 0 and a,
the potential is 0.

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:49.250
And get a negative b to
0 is the potential u0.

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:51.950
So I have two different regions.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:22:04.735
One is-- and minus
E psi equals 0.

00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:12.040
And the other is--
so this is between--

00:22:12.040 --> 00:22:16.450
for x, it's between a and 0.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:21.160
The other is for x
between 0 and negative b.

00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:24.370
And in that region, my
Schrodinger equation

00:22:24.370 --> 00:22:36.040
is 2m d plus psi d x square
plus u0 minus E psi equals 0.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:38.860
So I have two regions.

00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:41.530
And, of course, I need
a boundary conditions.

00:22:41.530 --> 00:22:44.260
In the end, what I'm
curious is still,

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:47.270
what are the energies
of the electron?

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:58.780
So we solved this type of a
problem in the last lecture.

00:22:58.780 --> 00:23:02.320
And, here is, let's
say, 5 at a height.

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:04.510
Before we say,
potentially infinite.

00:23:04.510 --> 00:23:07.720
So in that region, the
wave function is 0.

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:11.050
But now I have final u0.

00:23:11.050 --> 00:23:15.830
So my wave function is
not 0 in this region.

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:18.310
So I'm going to
solve the first one.

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:19.390
Let's write the equation.

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:27.620
Yesterday I was using small k.

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:29.660
But today let me
switch to a capital

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:35.280
K. Capital K is K
square wave function.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:39.560
So this is for this region--

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:42.050
for between 0 and a.

00:23:45.284 --> 00:23:49.650
And K square is same location.

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:52.380
I want to find that
if I put this together

00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:57.690
is 2mE divided by h bar square.

00:23:57.690 --> 00:23:58.568
That's K square.

00:24:01.990 --> 00:24:05.290
And I'm going to solve this.

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:08.510
You know the solution already.

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:15.310
So in this region, 0, a, my
wave function as function of x

00:24:15.310 --> 00:24:18.880
is A exponential minus iK--

00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:30.260
capital K x plus B exponential
plus i capital K x.

00:24:33.010 --> 00:24:39.850
So this is one region that
I'm interested in, 0 to a.

00:24:39.850 --> 00:24:42.775
The other region is
from minus b to 0.

00:24:45.670 --> 00:24:48.010
If you look at the equation
there [INAUDIBLE] is

00:24:48.010 --> 00:24:53.223
a plus, u0 minus E. Of course,
you can write that, also,

00:24:53.223 --> 00:24:54.140
into [INAUDIBLE] here.

00:24:54.140 --> 00:24:55.380
You can do the same.

00:24:55.380 --> 00:25:02.120
But let me-- if my [INAUDIBLE]
Q square equals 2M u0

00:25:02.120 --> 00:25:06.140
minus E divided by h square.

00:25:06.140 --> 00:25:09.470
So K square is 2mE h square.

00:25:09.470 --> 00:25:11.280
Now E is negative.

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:16.880
So my solution-- my root then
is a plus or minus [INAUDIBLE]..

00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:20.180
It's another plus or minus iK.

00:25:20.180 --> 00:25:24.170
That's the characteristic
equation for this one.

00:25:24.170 --> 00:25:32.270
And then-- solution then
is exponential minus Qx

00:25:32.270 --> 00:25:35.210
plus D exponential plus Qx.

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:46.190
You can write into
i if you reverse

00:25:46.190 --> 00:25:50.050
E and the U, your choice.

00:25:50.050 --> 00:25:51.970
It doesn't matter.

00:25:51.970 --> 00:25:55.840
At the end, as long as you're
consistent after your mass,

00:25:55.840 --> 00:25:57.560
you're fine.

00:25:57.560 --> 00:26:02.610
So what I want to find
out is [INAUDIBLE] E.

00:26:02.610 --> 00:26:04.600
This is my target.

00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:07.600
What are the energy
of the electron?

00:26:07.600 --> 00:26:08.875
It's an eigenvalue problem.

00:26:11.850 --> 00:26:15.360
So I need to look
at the solution

00:26:15.360 --> 00:26:19.640
and give a boundary
condition to the problem

00:26:19.640 --> 00:26:21.180
so that I can solve for--

00:26:21.180 --> 00:26:23.690
eventually I want
to solve for E.

00:26:23.690 --> 00:26:27.890
So what are my boundary
between minus b to a?

00:26:27.890 --> 00:26:32.390
The interface here between
the two region x equals 0--

00:26:32.390 --> 00:26:34.820
there's a boundary.

00:26:34.820 --> 00:26:37.190
At this location,
the wave function

00:26:37.190 --> 00:26:39.960
itself has to be continuous.

00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:43.050
And, also, I tell you the
derivative of wave function

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:46.060
has to be continuous.

00:26:46.060 --> 00:26:49.690
And I'm not going to
demonstrate to prove it.

00:26:49.690 --> 00:26:53.290
But, basically, if you say
your particle flux expression

00:26:53.290 --> 00:26:54.800
that we had before--

00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:57.670
if you require the particle
flux has to be continuous.

00:26:57.670 --> 00:26:59.170
If your wave function
is continuous,

00:26:59.170 --> 00:27:03.460
your derivatives also
has to be continuous.

00:27:03.460 --> 00:27:08.950
So my-- either x equals 0,
what I have is this wave

00:27:08.950 --> 00:27:11.710
function is continuous.

00:27:11.710 --> 00:27:14.560
So on the two sides, the
wave function is continuous.

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:15.640
What do I have?

00:27:15.640 --> 00:27:25.000
I have A plus B equals plus D.

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:26.950
Now you say I will require--

00:27:26.950 --> 00:27:29.350
I will need four
boundary conditions.

00:27:32.660 --> 00:27:38.250
And first order derivative
has to be continuous.

00:27:38.250 --> 00:27:48.800
So what I have is iK
and minus A plus B--

00:27:48.800 --> 00:27:52.190
that's the derivative
at x go towards 0--

00:27:52.190 --> 00:28:00.870
equals Q minus C
plus D. Those are

00:28:00.870 --> 00:28:06.100
the continuity at x equal to 0.

00:28:06.100 --> 00:28:10.710
Now I have two
boundary conditions.

00:28:10.710 --> 00:28:11.670
I need two more.

00:28:14.390 --> 00:28:16.370
So this is where--

00:28:16.370 --> 00:28:18.800
I mentioned at the beginning--

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:21.890
the Bloch theorem
start to kick in.

00:28:21.890 --> 00:28:23.240
Why?

00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:27.350
The problem is if I just write
this two boundary condition,

00:28:27.350 --> 00:28:29.540
it's just a single interface.

00:28:29.540 --> 00:28:32.390
It doesn't-- it has-- it
bears nothing to do with

00:28:32.390 --> 00:28:35.960
the periodicity of the crystal.

00:28:35.960 --> 00:28:41.030
Now, if you go back
to the potential--

00:28:41.030 --> 00:28:44.150
the u potential is
a function of x.

00:28:44.150 --> 00:28:48.380
Of course, in the problem we
have here is a step function.

00:28:48.380 --> 00:28:49.370
We use a square.

00:28:49.370 --> 00:28:52.430
So it's a step function,
in general, any arbitrary

00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:53.240
function.

00:28:53.240 --> 00:28:58.820
But it's a periodic
so ux equals u x

00:28:58.820 --> 00:29:05.600
plus T. That's the periodicity.

00:29:05.600 --> 00:29:11.070
So if you use this periodicity
and you go to the Schrodinger

00:29:11.070 --> 00:29:16.480
equation, and you ask,
what does this periodicity

00:29:16.480 --> 00:29:18.160
bring you to the solution?

00:29:18.160 --> 00:29:21.520
What's the requirement
for your solution?

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:24.880
And then mathematically,
the Bloch Theorem--

00:29:24.880 --> 00:29:30.050
Bloch proved that because of
this potential periodicity,

00:29:30.050 --> 00:29:41.340
my wave function-- so
due to periodicity,

00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:45.270
the wave function has to be--

00:29:45.270 --> 00:29:49.355
after-- so wave
function x plus T later.

00:29:52.230 --> 00:29:55.530
So one period later,
the same location

00:29:55.530 --> 00:30:01.860
is related to the wave
function of x previous period,

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:14.900
same location, by ik times
T. So this k is a small k.

00:30:14.900 --> 00:30:17.780
And that's the
Bloch Theorem here.

00:30:17.780 --> 00:30:22.800
And, in fact, you can write
this in more general term.

00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:28.250
And, so here-- this is a 1D.

00:30:28.250 --> 00:30:31.430
And there are 3D version,
which we will comment later on.

00:30:31.430 --> 00:30:39.870
And this small k
is a wave vector

00:30:39.870 --> 00:30:43.810
that we'll discuss
more later on.

00:30:43.810 --> 00:30:49.300
That's why I'm using
capital K for the solution

00:30:49.300 --> 00:30:51.970
and to distinguish from
the small k with a vector.

00:30:54.730 --> 00:31:01.090
So what does this tell us is,
I'm going to use a periodicity.

00:31:01.090 --> 00:31:03.160
Now, I can look at this point--

00:31:05.830 --> 00:31:07.510
this point.

00:31:07.510 --> 00:31:12.880
And in the left-hand side is
my solution between 0 to a.

00:31:12.880 --> 00:31:15.670
On the right-hand
side is this point.

00:31:15.670 --> 00:31:18.760
This point is this one--

00:31:18.760 --> 00:31:20.870
[INAUDIBLE]

00:31:20.870 --> 00:31:24.350
And I have a solution for
this-- to this region.

00:31:24.350 --> 00:31:25.980
I have a solution
for this region.

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:30.100
So I just need to relate
through this solution

00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:32.710
through the Bloch Theorem.

00:31:32.710 --> 00:31:36.160
So either x square to a,
I use the Bloch Theorem.

00:31:39.900 --> 00:31:43.260
x equal to a, the
Bloch Theorem say

00:31:43.260 --> 00:31:47.050
the wave function is related
and also corresponding.

00:31:47.050 --> 00:31:48.000
You take a derivative.

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:49.470
Derivative is also related.

00:31:52.050 --> 00:31:56.856
So the wave function is A--

00:31:56.856 --> 00:31:59.680
in the first region, 0 to a--

00:31:59.680 --> 00:32:01.830
you see, we have
that solution is

00:32:01.830 --> 00:32:09.330
a exponential to minus
i capital A Ka plus B

00:32:09.330 --> 00:32:13.710
exponential positive Ka.

00:32:13.710 --> 00:32:18.390
And this equal to
exponential i k--

00:32:18.390 --> 00:32:24.390
small k-- times T. That's
the T equals A plus B.

00:32:24.390 --> 00:32:27.930
And then times the
wave function when

00:32:27.930 --> 00:32:32.010
x equals to minus B. So
if I do x equals minus B

00:32:32.010 --> 00:32:35.850
in that region, must be to 0.

00:32:35.850 --> 00:32:39.090
So when x square
to it must be is

00:32:39.090 --> 00:32:44.884
exponential Q of b plus D
exponential minus Q of b.

00:32:48.990 --> 00:32:50.850
So I got my third equation.

00:32:50.850 --> 00:32:53.550
And, similarly, if
I take a derivative,

00:32:53.550 --> 00:32:55.810
I got my fourth equation.

00:32:55.810 --> 00:32:59.940
So this is the wave
function, Bloch theorem,

00:32:59.940 --> 00:33:02.550
and derivative,
Bloch theorem again.

00:33:02.550 --> 00:33:06.030
So derivative is-- if
I take the derivative,

00:33:06.030 --> 00:33:07.570
you can say they're equal.

00:33:07.570 --> 00:33:25.550
So I have iKa and A exponential
minus exponential iKa plus B

00:33:25.550 --> 00:33:30.680
exponential plus Ka--
this is a capital--

00:33:30.680 --> 00:33:35.390
equals exponential minus iKT.

00:33:35.390 --> 00:33:50.370
And you have a Q in the front
and minus exponential Qb plus D

00:33:50.370 --> 00:33:52.950
exponential negative Qb.

00:33:56.080 --> 00:33:59.590
We're not going to do more
operation of those four

00:33:59.590 --> 00:34:00.790
equations.

00:34:00.790 --> 00:34:03.460
The point I want to make is--

00:34:03.460 --> 00:34:08.820
if you look at this, it's
a homogeneous equation,

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:10.894
no constant terms.

00:34:10.894 --> 00:34:14.480
A, B, C, D-- you have
four coefficients.

00:34:14.480 --> 00:34:17.270
And no constant terms
if you move to the one

00:34:17.270 --> 00:34:20.460
side or constant is 0.

00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:25.400
So this is the characteristics
of eigenvalue equations.

00:34:25.400 --> 00:34:29.960
And you are-- if you have
a homogeneous equation,

00:34:29.960 --> 00:34:31.850
to have a long zero solution--

00:34:31.850 --> 00:34:35.929
A, B, C, D-- your determinant
must be 0 for linear equations.

00:34:39.590 --> 00:34:41.540
Everybody's following me?

00:34:41.540 --> 00:34:44.120
The determinant of--

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:48.489
1, 2, 3, 4 is 0.

00:34:48.489 --> 00:34:52.780
If you say there's a determinant
0, you look at this--

00:34:52.780 --> 00:34:57.940
capital K is a
function of energy.

00:34:57.940 --> 00:35:05.080
K is a function of
energy E. And capital Q

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:06.430
is a function of energy.

00:35:06.430 --> 00:35:08.245
So capital Q is a
function of energy.

00:35:11.120 --> 00:35:15.770
So given the A, given the B--

00:35:15.770 --> 00:35:21.350
we know T. And for each k, I
have a solution for energy.

00:35:21.350 --> 00:35:25.940
So this is where my
math will end up.

00:35:25.940 --> 00:35:30.380
So because this is a
homogeneous equation,

00:35:30.380 --> 00:35:38.510
my determinant must be
0, the coefficients.

00:35:38.510 --> 00:35:41.640
You put all your
coefficients together,

00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:43.910
and you will get
an equation that

00:35:43.910 --> 00:35:49.360
allow you to determine the
energy levels of the electron

00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:51.312
in such a periodical potential.

00:35:54.650 --> 00:35:59.760
So let me do a
few steps of math.

00:35:59.760 --> 00:36:09.010
And if you do the
determinant, you

00:36:09.010 --> 00:36:16.090
will actually will get an
equation not that scary--

00:36:16.090 --> 00:36:20.260
is Q square minus K
square-- capital--

00:36:20.260 --> 00:36:27.520
and a 2KQ sinh function--

00:36:27.520 --> 00:36:33.130
hyperbolic sin-- Qb and sine--

00:36:33.130 --> 00:36:45.760
real sine-- Ka plus cosh Qb
and the cosine capital K a.

00:36:45.760 --> 00:36:50.710
On the right-hand side
is cosine small k--

00:36:50.710 --> 00:36:52.510
that's a wave vector--

00:36:52.510 --> 00:36:53.530
a plus b.

00:36:53.530 --> 00:37:00.920
That's the periodical
at T. So this is the--

00:37:00.920 --> 00:37:06.530
if you do your determinant of
this full equation, at the end,

00:37:06.530 --> 00:37:09.890
you get this set of
equation, this equation here.

00:37:09.890 --> 00:37:12.340
In this equation, Q has energy.

00:37:12.340 --> 00:37:14.030
K has energy.

00:37:14.030 --> 00:37:17.360
And small k-- so
for each k value,

00:37:17.360 --> 00:37:20.135
you can solve for that
energy in the equation.

00:37:24.190 --> 00:37:30.280
And this-- still, it's
not very graphical.

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:32.980
Mathematically, it's
still too complicated.

00:37:32.980 --> 00:37:35.680
So let me make one
more simplification

00:37:35.680 --> 00:37:39.970
for the purpose of
explaining this solution will

00:37:39.970 --> 00:37:43.660
lead to the band
gap in the material.

00:37:43.660 --> 00:37:46.476
The band gap is, essentially, if
you think about semiconductors

00:37:46.476 --> 00:37:48.700
and all those.

00:37:48.700 --> 00:37:55.690
So, my next step is
I let b close to 0.

00:37:55.690 --> 00:37:58.780
But say, I will keep U times b--

00:37:58.780 --> 00:38:05.010
because when that b is 0,
this is a very lateral--

00:38:05.010 --> 00:38:06.220
b is [INAUDIBLE].

00:38:06.220 --> 00:38:08.730
So this becomes very lateral.

00:38:08.730 --> 00:38:12.390
And U times b finite.

00:38:12.390 --> 00:38:19.660
That also means the potential
is going to shoot up very high.

00:38:19.660 --> 00:38:26.940
But with this, if I say
b close to 0 Q times b,

00:38:26.940 --> 00:38:30.990
this gets to just
approximate that Qb itself.

00:38:30.990 --> 00:38:32.310
[INAUDIBLE] it.

00:38:32.310 --> 00:38:36.000
So this-- by that,
the Q and Q cancel.

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:41.220
So what I have here, I
can write as P capital

00:38:41.220 --> 00:38:50.040
K times a sine capital K times
a and plus cosine capital

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:55.380
K times a equals cosine ka.

00:38:55.380 --> 00:38:57.090
Because b is 0.

00:38:57.090 --> 00:39:00.030
So a, itself, is
the periodicity.

00:39:00.030 --> 00:39:01.500
This is wave vector.

00:39:01.500 --> 00:39:03.150
This K has the energy.

00:39:03.150 --> 00:39:08.160
And the P, itself,
is just a constant.

00:39:08.160 --> 00:39:09.570
P here is a constant.

00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:19.530
So this one-- with this, I
can go say graphically what

00:39:19.530 --> 00:39:21.210
this solution will look like.

00:39:23.790 --> 00:39:29.060
You can say now, the
left-hand side is the cosine.

00:39:29.060 --> 00:39:32.990
The maximum is the
minus 1 to plus 1.

00:39:32.990 --> 00:39:34.280
The right-hand side--

00:39:34.280 --> 00:39:40.740
I want to find the energy K.
And this capital K has energy.

00:39:40.740 --> 00:39:46.140
Capital K is 2mE h square.

00:39:46.140 --> 00:39:51.760
So you can say, this is
between minus 1 to 1.

00:39:51.760 --> 00:39:55.530
And here is a factor--

00:39:55.530 --> 00:39:59.430
when Ka goes to 1,
this divide this.

00:39:59.430 --> 00:40:01.950
Sine x divided by x is 1.

00:40:01.950 --> 00:40:04.290
So it's a P plus--

00:40:04.290 --> 00:40:06.180
so this could be larger than 1.

00:40:06.180 --> 00:40:09.420
In that case, there
is no solution.

00:40:09.420 --> 00:40:13.660
There's no K-- capital K--
with the-- satisfy that.

00:40:13.660 --> 00:40:17.385
So, graphically, If I do my
solution, what it looks like--

00:40:36.920 --> 00:40:43.090
So what I'm going to
draw here on the--

00:40:43.090 --> 00:40:44.710
is as a function of Ka.

00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:48.630
So here I have K--

00:40:48.630 --> 00:40:52.090
capital K-- a.

00:40:52.090 --> 00:40:59.050
And because this is a little
bit difficult to solve.

00:40:59.050 --> 00:41:02.890
So here is that function
on the left-hand side.

00:41:06.070 --> 00:41:11.250
On the left-hand
side, it's just a--

00:41:11.250 --> 00:41:13.086
you enter a decrease
into cosine.

00:41:18.240 --> 00:41:18.740
OK?

00:41:18.740 --> 00:41:19.670
AUDIENCE: Yes.

00:41:19.670 --> 00:41:23.450
PROFESSOR: And on
the-- so this is Ka.

00:41:23.450 --> 00:41:25.970
And on the right-hand side is--

00:41:25.970 --> 00:41:29.000
the range is minus 1 to plus 1.

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:33.860
So because I want to find that
one other solution K for that

00:41:33.860 --> 00:41:38.750
include energy-- so
this is the range

00:41:38.750 --> 00:41:41.330
between minus 1 to plus 1.

00:41:41.330 --> 00:41:42.480
I'm not drawing well.

00:41:42.480 --> 00:41:44.090
So this is a positive 1.

00:41:44.090 --> 00:41:45.380
This is negative 1.

00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:49.430
So that means when K in this
region, I have solution.

00:41:49.430 --> 00:41:51.530
In this region, I have solution.

00:41:51.530 --> 00:41:55.190
In this region, I have solution.

00:41:55.190 --> 00:41:58.960
But as the Ka becomes
larger, eventually, this

00:41:58.960 --> 00:42:01.240
is within minus 1 to plus 1.

00:42:01.240 --> 00:42:04.150
So I have a solution
everywhere when

00:42:04.150 --> 00:42:06.490
this Ka becomes very large.

00:42:06.490 --> 00:42:08.750
Ka means, again, energy.

00:42:08.750 --> 00:42:11.620
So that means when
energy is very large,

00:42:11.620 --> 00:42:13.240
I don't have forbidden region.

00:42:13.240 --> 00:42:18.220
But in this region,
this is my forbidden--

00:42:18.220 --> 00:42:20.485
I don't have any
energy in this region.

00:42:23.720 --> 00:42:25.535
This region, I don't
have a solution.

00:42:33.460 --> 00:42:36.940
So if I replot this--

00:42:36.940 --> 00:42:42.250
because what I'm saying here
is, this region for any ka--

00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:44.470
cosine the small k a--

00:42:44.470 --> 00:42:47.770
if you gave me a values of
the cosine and small k a,

00:42:47.770 --> 00:42:51.080
I have a corresponding
energy solution.

00:42:51.080 --> 00:42:54.290
So I can go replot
that ka because this

00:42:54.290 --> 00:42:56.130
is a periodical function.

00:42:56.130 --> 00:42:59.360
So, now, this is a capital
K. That gives me energy.

00:42:59.360 --> 00:43:04.785
My [INAUDIBLE] is I'm going to
plot this function in small k

00:43:04.785 --> 00:43:06.056
a.

00:43:06.056 --> 00:43:07.670
I hope you don't get confused.

00:43:10.500 --> 00:43:15.320
I'm going to plot out what
the solution look like.

00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:21.340
And the solution is say--

00:43:21.340 --> 00:43:23.590
because this is a cosine ka--

00:43:23.590 --> 00:43:25.120
so it's a periodic.

00:43:25.120 --> 00:43:27.325
So my solution will
look like this.

00:43:39.590 --> 00:43:41.470
And this is the energy.

00:43:41.470 --> 00:43:46.195
And, essentially, what that
energy has is derived from k.

00:43:46.195 --> 00:43:49.390
And so capital K a
is in this region.

00:43:49.390 --> 00:43:51.740
That's [INAUDIBLE] solution.

00:43:51.740 --> 00:43:54.250
And so this is a--

00:43:54.250 --> 00:43:55.990
if in this region--

00:43:55.990 --> 00:43:58.990
and in the next region,
I don't have energy.

00:43:58.990 --> 00:43:59.950
This is a forbidden.

00:43:59.950 --> 00:44:02.260
So I can't-- for the--

00:44:02.260 --> 00:44:09.140
when in this region of energy
here, there's no solution.

00:44:09.140 --> 00:44:12.800
So there is a gap here.

00:44:12.800 --> 00:44:15.710
Because this is beyond the 1.

00:44:15.710 --> 00:44:19.205
So what I have is [INAUDIBLE]
what it looks like.

00:44:33.630 --> 00:44:37.040
So in between is a gap.

00:44:37.040 --> 00:44:42.200
This is the gap that
I've been talking.

00:44:42.200 --> 00:44:45.570
That's the corresponding
to this region here,

00:44:45.570 --> 00:44:50.090
I have no solution,
no allowable energy.

00:44:50.090 --> 00:44:52.880
Electrons cannot have
this energy when they put

00:44:52.880 --> 00:44:55.156
in the periodic structure.

00:44:59.840 --> 00:45:03.200
So this is my--

00:45:03.200 --> 00:45:05.790
how the solution will look like.

00:45:05.790 --> 00:45:09.080
And then let's leave
here and come back

00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:12.920
to look at this wave vector.

00:45:12.920 --> 00:45:16.655
What is the allowable
wave vector values?

00:45:20.460 --> 00:45:28.980
So for the wave vector, I
have to go back to the--

00:45:28.980 --> 00:45:33.180
here-- this is
the Bloch Theorem.

00:45:33.180 --> 00:45:40.590
And so I need to decide,
what is the wave vector?

00:45:40.590 --> 00:45:45.490
And I now-- I have for
any atoms in the crystal--

00:45:45.490 --> 00:45:49.403
so between 1 and the
capital N, the total length

00:45:49.403 --> 00:45:50.070
of the crystal--

00:45:53.140 --> 00:45:56.800
L, the length of the
crystal is the N atoms

00:45:56.800 --> 00:45:59.530
times the periodicity.

00:45:59.530 --> 00:46:02.920
And this periodicity--
and the limit I'm consider

00:46:02.920 --> 00:46:06.860
is N times a. a is my period.

00:46:06.860 --> 00:46:07.715
Because b is 0.

00:46:12.230 --> 00:46:19.910
So this is where there is
a very interesting boundary

00:46:19.910 --> 00:46:24.230
condition, sort of artificial
boundary condition,

00:46:24.230 --> 00:46:26.120
that was introduced.

00:46:26.120 --> 00:46:30.320
And this boundary
condition is-- this is a 1.

00:46:30.320 --> 00:46:35.660
This is an M. That's a
finite-length crystal.

00:46:35.660 --> 00:46:38.480
There is a finite length.

00:46:38.480 --> 00:46:43.970
And von Karman introduced a
periodic boundary condition.

00:46:47.130 --> 00:46:48.990
Now I'm going to
write von Karman.

00:46:56.490 --> 00:46:59.160
And what I say is--

00:46:59.160 --> 00:47:02.980
because this N, capital
N, is usually very large,

00:47:02.980 --> 00:47:05.530
it really doesn't matter much.

00:47:05.530 --> 00:47:08.745
And the one way to do-- to say
a periodic boundary condition

00:47:08.745 --> 00:47:13.690
is say, after this 1 to N, the
crystal will repeat itself.

00:47:13.690 --> 00:47:17.940
So N plus 1 come back to 1.

00:47:17.940 --> 00:47:22.470
So what is the
wave function for n

00:47:22.470 --> 00:47:30.410
plus 1 equals the wave
function of 1 first atom.

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:35.200
And your real space
is going from 1 to N.

00:47:35.200 --> 00:47:37.990
And this is called the von
Karman periodical boundary

00:47:37.990 --> 00:47:40.060
condition.

00:47:40.060 --> 00:47:47.380
And what does that
tell us is when--

00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:55.660
so what we have here
is, when x equals n--

00:47:55.660 --> 00:48:07.390
so what I have is
for psi x plus Na--

00:48:07.390 --> 00:48:10.780
that's the length
of the crystal--

00:48:10.780 --> 00:48:14.890
is equals psi x here.

00:48:17.740 --> 00:48:34.430
And, with that, I will
have exponential ik times

00:48:34.430 --> 00:48:39.770
Na should equal to 1.

00:48:39.770 --> 00:48:42.950
So this is what from Karman
periodic boundary condition

00:48:42.950 --> 00:48:43.880
gives me.

00:48:43.880 --> 00:48:53.960
And it gives me a way to
say k equals 2 pi Na--

00:48:53.960 --> 00:48:56.170
that's the length
of the crystal--

00:48:56.170 --> 00:48:59.260
and times a small n.

00:48:59.260 --> 00:49:05.590
And this n is plus or
minus 1, plus or minus 2,

00:49:05.590 --> 00:49:08.333
and plus or minus n.

00:49:08.333 --> 00:49:08.875
You continue.

00:49:13.190 --> 00:49:18.440
Now, what it means is
this small k wave vector

00:49:18.440 --> 00:49:21.650
is not a continuous function.

00:49:21.650 --> 00:49:27.170
It has-- if you look at this n,
when error n equals the length

00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:29.690
of the crystal--

00:49:29.690 --> 00:49:36.490
when n equals capital
N and I have the ka--

00:49:36.490 --> 00:49:42.020
k times a-- we'll
repeat the 2 pi.

00:49:42.020 --> 00:49:44.680
k-- if you look
at that small k--

00:49:44.680 --> 00:49:49.330
k times a, when n
equals to capital

00:49:49.330 --> 00:49:53.020
n-- small n equal to
capital N-- that's 2 pi.

00:49:53.020 --> 00:49:56.110
So here what I
have is, this is 0.

00:49:56.110 --> 00:49:57.640
This is 2 pi.

00:49:57.640 --> 00:50:03.590
And between ka-- between 0 and
2 pi, I have, really, endpoints.

00:50:03.590 --> 00:50:06.100
So I will have--

00:50:06.100 --> 00:50:13.040
the number of points
is N points here.

00:50:13.040 --> 00:50:16.610
N is the number of
atoms in the crystal.

00:50:22.210 --> 00:50:25.400
I think the other way
I want to say this--

00:50:25.400 --> 00:50:27.655
from Karman periodic
boundary condition,

00:50:27.655 --> 00:50:29.770
it really doesn't matter.

00:50:29.770 --> 00:50:34.180
Basically, I have
electrons that extend--

00:50:34.180 --> 00:50:37.450
the wave function can be
extended between 1 and n.

00:50:40.330 --> 00:50:47.110
I have a wave function
in the region of 0

00:50:47.110 --> 00:50:50.650
to L. Because I say
this is my beginning.

00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:54.230
The [INAUDIBLE] L
is the total length.

00:50:54.230 --> 00:51:01.490
So now I ask you, if you know
a function, whatever function,

00:51:01.490 --> 00:51:04.190
between 0 and L--

00:51:04.190 --> 00:51:07.960
x equals 0 to L--

00:51:07.960 --> 00:51:13.590
and you know you can
do a Fourier series.

00:51:13.590 --> 00:51:17.620
This is a finite lens function.

00:51:17.620 --> 00:51:20.440
If you don't recall
your Fourier series--

00:51:20.440 --> 00:51:25.270
if you have a function between
0 to L you write into Fourier

00:51:25.270 --> 00:51:27.130
series sum, what is it?

00:51:32.770 --> 00:51:34.910
Huh?

00:51:34.910 --> 00:51:43.110
psi x-- any function
between 0 to L,

00:51:43.110 --> 00:51:44.940
you can decompose
into the series

00:51:44.940 --> 00:51:49.030
of sine and cosine functions.

00:51:49.030 --> 00:51:50.570
So let's write that.

00:51:50.570 --> 00:51:52.690
So I have, in
general, any function.

00:51:52.690 --> 00:51:59.160
I can always write
a0 plus sigma n

00:51:59.160 --> 00:52:11.360
equals 1 to infinite a
n cosine 2 pi n over L

00:52:11.360 --> 00:52:22.690
x and plus bn sine 2 pi n L x.

00:52:22.690 --> 00:52:27.220
That's any function-- as long as
I know this function between 0

00:52:27.220 --> 00:52:31.810
to L, I can expand it in
sine and cosine series.

00:52:34.370 --> 00:52:36.300
You agree?

00:52:36.300 --> 00:52:39.590
So, what does this tell me?

00:52:39.590 --> 00:52:44.790
If I write sine
cosine in exponential

00:52:44.790 --> 00:52:55.450
is a n complex and
exponential i 2 pi n

00:52:55.450 --> 00:53:05.788
L x plus bn complex and
exponential minus i 2 pi n L x.

00:53:08.560 --> 00:53:12.170
I can rearrange and
write into exponential.

00:53:12.170 --> 00:53:16.840
Once I write into exponential,
what does this mean?

00:53:16.840 --> 00:53:20.820
This is the stationary part
of the Schrodinger equation.

00:53:20.820 --> 00:53:23.460
You remember there is a
time-dependent exponential

00:53:23.460 --> 00:53:27.900
minus i omega T. If I put
a minus i omega T into this

00:53:27.900 --> 00:53:33.100
and multiply together,
this is a wave propagating

00:53:33.100 --> 00:53:35.470
to the positive x direction.

00:53:35.470 --> 00:53:41.960
This is a wave propagating
to the negative x direction.

00:53:41.960 --> 00:53:47.690
So I'm decomposing this wave
function into many modes.

00:53:47.690 --> 00:53:49.160
Again, the modes--

00:53:49.160 --> 00:53:50.600
2 pi n L--

00:53:50.600 --> 00:53:53.180
each n is one wave--

00:53:53.180 --> 00:53:56.490
one wavelength.

00:53:56.490 --> 00:54:00.180
So I'm decomposing
this into many modes.

00:54:00.180 --> 00:54:08.250
And so what I have is, every
2 pi, I will have a capital--

00:54:08.250 --> 00:54:10.230
a total [INAUDIBLE] endpoints.

00:54:13.970 --> 00:54:18.920
And it's very important to
understand this [INAUDIBLE]..

00:54:18.920 --> 00:54:22.190
So, basically, even though
this function I'm drawing

00:54:22.190 --> 00:54:29.930
is continuous, and I have many
very closely spaced points,

00:54:29.930 --> 00:54:31.970
as wave vectors.

00:54:31.970 --> 00:54:37.670
And the total between 0 to
pi, say ka when at 0 to pi

00:54:37.670 --> 00:54:39.680
is a capital endpoint states.

00:54:43.200 --> 00:54:50.100
So this is the
representation in terms

00:54:50.100 --> 00:54:53.880
of-- because it's periodic, so
now I have the option because I

00:54:53.880 --> 00:54:55.830
don't want to draw all this.

00:54:55.830 --> 00:54:57.630
So I can take a 0 to 2 pi.

00:54:57.630 --> 00:54:58.335
I can draw this.

00:55:01.157 --> 00:55:01.740
That's enough.

00:55:05.440 --> 00:55:09.400
But say, even this
is not the easier way

00:55:09.400 --> 00:55:12.620
to draw the band structure.

00:55:12.620 --> 00:55:16.720
And, in fact, people don't
like to draw 0 to pi.

00:55:16.720 --> 00:55:22.120
They like to draw 0 to pi
and the 0 to negative pi.

00:55:22.120 --> 00:55:25.580
Any two pi is fine.

00:55:25.580 --> 00:55:31.980
So I can draw, really, between
here and here, and forget

00:55:31.980 --> 00:55:32.480
the rest.

00:55:36.570 --> 00:55:39.110
And that's one.

00:55:39.110 --> 00:55:40.660
And even this from--

00:55:40.660 --> 00:55:45.920
from negative pi to positive
pi, again, there are endpoints.

00:55:45.920 --> 00:55:47.120
0 to pi, they are endpoints.

00:55:47.120 --> 00:55:52.170
And negative pi to the pi,
they are also endpoints.

00:55:52.170 --> 00:55:55.880
But say it's a symmetric.

00:55:55.880 --> 00:56:00.380
The wave going forward positive
x direction and negative x

00:56:00.380 --> 00:56:03.320
direction-- they are symmetric.

00:56:03.320 --> 00:56:09.100
That's why my solution positive
k [INAUDIBLE] is symmetric.

00:56:09.100 --> 00:56:15.890
So because of that, I only
draw half, so 0 to pi.

00:56:15.890 --> 00:56:18.920
So that's usually
what you say when

00:56:18.920 --> 00:56:22.190
people plot the band structure.

00:56:22.190 --> 00:56:27.770
And this-- what they'll say is--

00:56:27.770 --> 00:56:29.630
they don't plot ka.

00:56:29.630 --> 00:56:31.760
They will plot here, 0 to pi.

00:56:31.760 --> 00:56:33.260
So this is pi over a.

00:56:33.260 --> 00:56:36.050
That's a k wave vector.

00:56:36.050 --> 00:56:38.660
And here is the energy.

00:56:38.660 --> 00:56:48.700
And this is the solution
for whatever potential

00:56:48.700 --> 00:56:53.821
in this specific periodicity
direction of the crystal.

00:56:53.821 --> 00:56:54.650
All right.

00:56:54.650 --> 00:56:58.820
I say it's a 1D crystal.

00:56:58.820 --> 00:57:01.220
In real crystal, is
every direction you look,

00:57:01.220 --> 00:57:04.160
you can say, OK I'm
considered the periodicity

00:57:04.160 --> 00:57:06.030
in that specific direction.

00:57:06.030 --> 00:57:07.520
And that's my wave vector.

00:57:07.520 --> 00:57:10.130
That's why now it's a vector.

00:57:10.130 --> 00:57:13.825
Wave vector direction is
along that specific direction

00:57:13.825 --> 00:57:14.450
of the crystal.

00:57:17.170 --> 00:57:19.840
And we will discuss
in the next lecture

00:57:19.840 --> 00:57:26.170
more on the crystal geometries
and different geometry

00:57:26.170 --> 00:57:28.690
of crystal.

00:57:28.690 --> 00:57:32.870
Remember, here, because
there is a 0 to pi--

00:57:32.870 --> 00:57:34.060
0 to pi only.

00:57:34.060 --> 00:57:41.350
So there are really a 1/2 n,
n over 2 points, between 0

00:57:41.350 --> 00:57:42.700
to pi away.

00:57:42.700 --> 00:57:45.220
Because there are
another 1/2 is begin

00:57:45.220 --> 00:57:50.110
on the other side, the negative
side, which I didn't draw.

00:57:52.890 --> 00:57:55.800
So what does it-- what's
so special out of those--

00:57:55.800 --> 00:57:58.870
[INAUDIBLE] electron
energy level.

00:57:58.870 --> 00:58:03.870
And this is-- so you have
this semicontinuous curve.

00:58:03.870 --> 00:58:05.880
The curve, itself,
you draw continuous.

00:58:05.880 --> 00:58:07.830
But then because of
k is discontinuous,

00:58:07.830 --> 00:58:11.790
this n is also
really closest space

00:58:11.790 --> 00:58:13.080
about this continuous point.

00:58:16.210 --> 00:58:19.090
What's the relation between
what we talked about for atomic

00:58:19.090 --> 00:58:21.740
[INAUDIBLE] at the beginning.

00:58:21.740 --> 00:58:25.890
And, roughly, this
bad is n equals 1.

00:58:25.890 --> 00:58:32.100
If I think about the hydrogen
atoms, negative 13.6 n square.

00:58:32.100 --> 00:58:33.840
And this band is n equals 1.

00:58:33.840 --> 00:58:35.130
This n equals 2.

00:58:35.130 --> 00:58:41.800
Now it's split into
many small levels.

00:58:41.800 --> 00:58:44.560
And we see-- at the beginning
when we discuss hydrogen--

00:58:44.560 --> 00:58:48.670
if I have any atoms,
I have energy levels.

00:58:48.670 --> 00:58:52.720
Now I have endpoints
between negative pi

00:58:52.720 --> 00:58:54.640
over a to plus pi over a.

00:58:54.640 --> 00:58:57.955
So I have n energy level
in each of the span.

00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:05.280
So, physically, it's a different
picture, different views.

00:59:05.280 --> 00:59:09.830
But they are all the same thing.

00:59:09.830 --> 00:59:14.400
Now, a few more
discussion here--

00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:16.580
discussion point.

00:59:16.580 --> 00:59:24.255
And first, we discuss
this small k with vector.

00:59:37.220 --> 00:59:44.030
One is the-- this
[INAUDIBLE] crystal h bar k.

00:59:44.030 --> 00:59:47.180
Remember, the
wave-particle duality

00:59:47.180 --> 00:59:51.890
is h over [INAUDIBLE]
h bar over k times k.

00:59:51.890 --> 00:59:53.590
And this is called
the-- in crystal,

00:59:53.590 --> 00:59:54.965
it's called the
crystal momentum.

01:00:05.170 --> 01:00:09.880
And without going
into detail, we can't.

01:00:09.880 --> 01:00:11.680
This is the momentum
when you think

01:00:11.680 --> 01:00:14.410
about doing the energy
conservation, momentum

01:00:14.410 --> 01:00:15.560
conservation.

01:00:15.560 --> 01:00:18.940
When two electrons
scatter with each other,

01:00:18.940 --> 01:00:22.630
they still have to obey
energy conservation.

01:00:22.630 --> 01:00:25.660
And they still have to obey
the momentum conservation.

01:00:25.660 --> 01:00:31.370
And this is the momentum
that we'll be using.

01:00:31.370 --> 01:00:36.370
And in 3D, k is a
vector that depends

01:00:36.370 --> 01:00:40.490
on different
crystallographic directions.

01:00:40.490 --> 01:00:47.616
And, also, we said that before,
this k and the k plus pi over a

01:00:47.616 --> 01:00:48.880
are equivalent.

01:00:48.880 --> 01:00:52.450
That's why we reduce this
periodical representation

01:00:52.450 --> 01:00:57.820
into only between negative
pi over a to plus pi over a.

01:00:57.820 --> 01:01:07.330
And what's really
striking is the gap.

01:01:07.330 --> 01:01:10.780
From this, we say-- there
you say at this region,

01:01:10.780 --> 01:01:12.520
there's no energy.

01:01:12.520 --> 01:01:14.200
There's no electron
in the crystal

01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:17.420
that can have those energy.

01:01:17.420 --> 01:01:19.040
And like here,
similarly, there's

01:01:19.040 --> 01:01:23.750
no electron in a crystal
that can have those energy.

01:01:23.750 --> 01:01:25.385
So we have an energy gap.

01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:38.150
And it turns out that
in real crystals,

01:01:38.150 --> 01:01:40.470
we have many
different directions.

01:01:40.470 --> 01:01:44.270
So maybe in one
direction is this way.

01:01:44.270 --> 01:01:47.540
Maybe another direction,
the potential is different.

01:01:47.540 --> 01:01:50.690
The periodicity--
this is a pi over a1.

01:01:50.690 --> 01:01:52.710
Periodicity in that direction.

01:01:52.710 --> 01:01:55.940
And maybe in the other
direction, is pi over a2.

01:01:55.940 --> 01:01:57.440
So it's not a--

01:01:57.440 --> 01:02:00.930
when I draw this, I'm drawing
in the other direction.

01:02:00.930 --> 01:02:01.910
It's not a negative.

01:02:01.910 --> 01:02:04.940
I'm just drawing in
the other direction.

01:02:04.940 --> 01:02:10.360
And it might be even having
the possibility of this way.

01:02:13.330 --> 01:02:16.030
And if I say in some
material it turns out

01:02:16.030 --> 01:02:20.470
that there is a
gap no matter what.

01:02:20.470 --> 01:02:24.190
consider all directions,
there is absolutely the region

01:02:24.190 --> 01:02:26.170
where there is no energy.

01:02:26.170 --> 01:02:29.305
And this is the band
gap of the material.

01:02:31.910 --> 01:02:36.740
So energy gap and the extension
is 3D is the band gap.

01:02:40.070 --> 01:02:44.370
Now, let's do a
little bit of counting

01:02:44.370 --> 01:02:48.800
and to say, what does this mean?

01:02:48.800 --> 01:02:51.700
So I take my hydrogen--

01:02:51.700 --> 01:02:56.160
one-dimensional hydrogen
chain as example.

01:02:56.160 --> 01:02:57.790
I put the electron--

01:02:57.790 --> 01:03:01.680
so if I have a hydrogen chain,
one-dimensional hydrogen chain,

01:03:01.680 --> 01:03:04.540
that's here.

01:03:04.540 --> 01:03:06.160
And I have not add spin.

01:03:06.160 --> 01:03:08.680
Now, I have to add spin.

01:03:08.680 --> 01:03:11.910
Spin is afterthought.

01:03:11.910 --> 01:03:14.290
Because my solution
doesn't include it.

01:03:14.290 --> 01:03:18.510
So each energy level, in
fact, there is an s plus--

01:03:18.510 --> 01:03:21.900
[INAUDIBLE] minus--
s 1/2 minus 1/2.

01:03:21.900 --> 01:03:24.680
So there are two quantum state.

01:03:24.680 --> 01:03:27.590
Now, I put the
electron-- electron

01:03:27.590 --> 01:03:32.090
or with anything
except the humans,

01:03:32.090 --> 01:03:33.980
like to go sit in the
lower energy state.

01:03:36.510 --> 01:03:40.440
And [INAUDIBLE] biological
systems may not.

01:03:40.440 --> 01:03:43.980
[INAUDIBLE] so I
put the electron

01:03:43.980 --> 01:03:45.360
to go to a lower-energy state.

01:03:48.170 --> 01:03:52.550
And if it's hydrogen--
so there are an electron.

01:03:52.550 --> 01:03:55.430
Each hydrogen has one electron.

01:03:55.430 --> 01:03:59.180
Between negative pi over
a to plus pi over a,

01:03:59.180 --> 01:04:01.410
I have endpoints.

01:04:01.410 --> 01:04:03.860
And that means I have
2n because of speed.

01:04:03.860 --> 01:04:06.480
I have 2n quantum state.

01:04:06.480 --> 01:04:09.950
So Pauli Exclusion
say each quantum state

01:04:09.950 --> 01:04:12.610
has maximum one electron.

01:04:12.610 --> 01:04:17.720
And, also, the Minimum Energy
Principle of Thermodynamics

01:04:17.720 --> 01:04:18.630
say--

01:04:18.630 --> 01:04:20.170
[INAUDIBLE] bring
in temperature.

01:04:20.170 --> 01:04:23.200
But thermodynamics say the
electron goes to lowest energy

01:04:23.200 --> 01:04:24.640
first.

01:04:24.640 --> 01:04:29.040
So what happens is now I have
electron go here, go here,

01:04:29.040 --> 01:04:32.190
go here, and fill in here.

01:04:32.190 --> 01:04:33.920
Because it's 1/2.

01:04:33.920 --> 01:04:34.850
I have 2n state.

01:04:34.850 --> 01:04:38.320
I have n electrons.

01:04:38.320 --> 01:04:46.000
So where electron fill to the
top, I say is-- this point

01:04:46.000 --> 01:04:49.195
is the Fermi surface,
Fermi energy, Fermi level.

01:04:52.460 --> 01:04:54.305
So we have Fermi level.

01:05:00.530 --> 01:05:01.030
This is Ef.

01:05:07.540 --> 01:05:10.870
And now, in just
a simple picture,

01:05:10.870 --> 01:05:13.870
electron fill to the 1/2.

01:05:13.870 --> 01:05:17.170
And now, if the
temperature is not 0,

01:05:17.170 --> 01:05:19.130
electron gather kT energy.

01:05:19.130 --> 01:05:22.160
Electron and the kT energy--

01:05:22.160 --> 01:05:25.520
those electron maybe
will be located.

01:05:25.520 --> 01:05:27.910
They don't move.

01:05:27.910 --> 01:05:33.070
Those electrons near the Fermi
surface, they have energy kT.

01:05:33.070 --> 01:05:36.550
And the energy separation
between these discrete small

01:05:36.550 --> 01:05:40.210
levels are small enough
so the thermal energy can

01:05:40.210 --> 01:05:43.570
make them move to other states.

01:05:43.570 --> 01:05:49.700
So electrons can
move in the band.

01:05:49.700 --> 01:05:52.980
So those are metals.

01:05:52.980 --> 01:05:58.560
In metal, the Fermi level
force into the bands.

01:05:58.560 --> 01:06:01.200
And in metal, not
every electron will be

01:06:01.200 --> 01:06:03.600
contributing to the conduction.

01:06:03.600 --> 01:06:06.120
AUDIENCE: What is so
special about Fermi levels?

01:06:06.120 --> 01:06:06.975
PROFESSOR: Huh?

01:06:06.975 --> 01:06:07.800
AUDIENCE: What is--

01:06:07.800 --> 01:06:10.092
PROFESSOR: Fermi level is
just a concept that will say,

01:06:10.092 --> 01:06:11.760
if I fill in,
where's the topmost?

01:06:11.760 --> 01:06:13.800
You fill in level in the bucket.

01:06:13.800 --> 01:06:15.600
Where is that surface there?

01:06:15.600 --> 01:06:19.180
That's where they
say those are--

01:06:19.180 --> 01:06:22.350
so electron-- only electron
near the Fermi level

01:06:22.350 --> 01:06:25.260
have a kT energy that
they can move around.

01:06:25.260 --> 01:06:29.670
The electron way below
the Fermi level, kT--

01:06:29.670 --> 01:06:32.440
the other stage isn't filled.

01:06:32.440 --> 01:06:34.620
So Pauli Exclusion
Principle say, no way.

01:06:34.620 --> 01:06:36.330
I don't allow you there.

01:06:36.330 --> 01:06:39.780
So the electrons
in this region--

01:06:39.780 --> 01:06:40.920
they don't contribute.

01:06:40.920 --> 01:06:43.590
So even metal-- you
say you're going

01:06:43.590 --> 01:06:46.950
to take a copper-- take a
lattice constant per unit

01:06:46.950 --> 01:06:48.270
will have many electron.

01:06:48.270 --> 01:06:50.850
But not all those
electrons will move,

01:06:50.850 --> 01:06:52.740
will contribute to conduction.

01:06:52.740 --> 01:06:56.590
Only the ones near
to the Fermi surface.

01:06:56.590 --> 01:07:00.130
AUDIENCE: So the Fermi
surface has to be [INAUDIBLE]??

01:07:00.130 --> 01:07:01.750
PROFESSOR: No, no, no.

01:07:01.750 --> 01:07:03.730
I take the hydrogen example.

01:07:03.730 --> 01:07:06.900
Now I'm going to
take a [INAUDIBLE]..

01:07:06.900 --> 01:07:11.170
Now what happens if
I do [INAUDIBLE]??

01:07:11.170 --> 01:07:12.530
Where is it?

01:07:12.530 --> 01:07:13.940
So this is going to be here.

01:07:13.940 --> 01:07:17.330
[INAUDIBLE] has two electrons.

01:07:17.330 --> 01:07:20.180
So I have two n states.

01:07:20.180 --> 01:07:24.400
I will fill to this region here.

01:07:24.400 --> 01:07:25.660
What happened?

01:07:25.660 --> 01:07:29.710
And that depends on
the gap here now.

01:07:29.710 --> 01:07:33.160
kT is 26 million
electron volts--

01:07:33.160 --> 01:07:35.920
26 million electron volts.

01:07:35.920 --> 01:07:40.360
And if the gap is a few electron
volts, 5 electron volts--

01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:49.300
so our field and the kT cannot
lift the electron to here.

01:07:49.300 --> 01:07:51.850
There is a real
forbidden region.

01:07:51.850 --> 01:07:55.250
Your electron cannot
have the energy.

01:07:55.250 --> 01:07:57.960
So now you have a gap.

01:07:57.960 --> 01:08:00.450
And this is the--

01:08:00.450 --> 01:08:03.600
in that case, if the
gap is really large--

01:08:03.600 --> 01:08:05.670
let's say 5 electron volts--

01:08:05.670 --> 01:08:06.900
it's an insulator.

01:08:06.900 --> 01:08:07.770
It's a dielectric.

01:08:07.770 --> 01:08:09.310
It's an insulator.

01:08:09.310 --> 01:08:10.185
You look like glass--

01:08:12.900 --> 01:08:15.270
the glass is an insulator
because there is

01:08:15.270 --> 01:08:18.200
a really large gap, energy gap.

01:08:18.200 --> 01:08:25.100
So photons-- with both
photon, the 0.5 micron.

01:08:25.100 --> 01:08:27.720
1 micron is 1.24.

01:08:27.720 --> 01:08:29.920
[SIGHS] I can't
remember which is which.

01:08:29.920 --> 01:08:33.569
1 electron is 1.24 micron.

01:08:33.569 --> 01:08:34.470
Or the 1/2--

01:08:34.470 --> 01:08:39.270
[INAUDIBLE] 0.5 microns is about
2-some electrons-- electron

01:08:39.270 --> 01:08:41.660
volts.

01:08:41.660 --> 01:08:46.359
2 electron volts-- the
gap is much larger.

01:08:46.359 --> 01:08:49.470
So the light will transmit
through the window.

01:08:49.470 --> 01:08:53.580
They [? can't ?] lock the
electron from here to here.

01:08:53.580 --> 01:08:55.740
They don't have enough energy.

01:08:55.740 --> 01:08:57.008
Yes?

01:08:57.008 --> 01:09:00.090
AUDIENCE: For semiconductors,
where the Fermi levels

01:09:00.090 --> 01:09:01.097
[INAUDIBLE] did--

01:09:01.097 --> 01:09:01.680
PROFESSOR: OK.

01:09:01.680 --> 01:09:02.450
AUDIENCE: --in the
[INAUDIBLE] gap--

01:09:02.450 --> 01:09:03.033
PROFESSOR: OK.

01:09:03.033 --> 01:09:04.229
That's-- you're jumping.

01:09:04.229 --> 01:09:05.272
AUDIENCE: How so?

01:09:05.272 --> 01:09:05.939
PROFESSOR: Good.

01:09:05.939 --> 01:09:06.870
Good question.

01:09:06.870 --> 01:09:12.750
I'm not-- so I have to go to
more talk about semiconductors.

01:09:12.750 --> 01:09:15.330
So semiconductor
gap is typically

01:09:15.330 --> 01:09:17.189
about 1 to 2 electron volts.

01:09:20.040 --> 01:09:23.010
And in that case, there are
some of the thermal energy--

01:09:23.010 --> 01:09:25.439
even though it's 26
million electron volts--

01:09:25.439 --> 01:09:27.930
I have not talked
about the [INAUDIBLE]----

01:09:27.930 --> 01:09:29.700
I mentioned [INAUDIBLE] Factor.

01:09:32.430 --> 01:09:36.210
So there is a distribution of
that energy-- thermal energy.

01:09:36.210 --> 01:09:40.160
Some electrons have
enough thermal energy--

01:09:40.160 --> 01:09:44.910
very few-- they can jump
if they have enough energy.

01:09:44.910 --> 01:09:48.750
Similarly, they can be
locked from here to here.

01:09:48.750 --> 01:09:50.990
So what happens--

01:09:50.990 --> 01:09:53.420
I'm talking about--
that's a 1D example.

01:09:53.420 --> 01:09:54.037
Here is 3D.

01:09:54.037 --> 01:09:54.620
It's the same.

01:09:54.620 --> 01:09:56.450
I have a gap.

01:09:56.450 --> 01:09:59.240
So some electrons can be
locked from here to here

01:09:59.240 --> 01:10:01.880
because if they have--
if those electrons have

01:10:01.880 --> 01:10:04.680
enough high energy
compared to the gap.

01:10:04.680 --> 01:10:07.340
So what's going to leave behind?

01:10:07.340 --> 01:10:11.000
If I have [AUDIO OUT]

01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:12.500
One more step.

01:10:12.500 --> 01:10:14.930
1, 2 helium.

01:10:14.930 --> 01:10:16.820
Go to the next one, lithium.

01:10:16.820 --> 01:10:17.930
it's 3 electron.

01:10:17.930 --> 01:10:22.570
It has to go to
here, the next band.

01:10:22.570 --> 01:10:24.790
And so the Fermi
level don't have

01:10:24.790 --> 01:10:26.020
to be lowest to [INAUDIBLE].

01:10:26.020 --> 01:10:27.130
It's just-- so
you have to fill--

01:10:27.130 --> 01:10:28.422
you look at the periodic table.

01:10:28.422 --> 01:10:30.425
You fill to the topmost.

01:10:30.425 --> 01:10:31.300
There are many bands.

01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:37.800
And so when we have the--

01:10:40.440 --> 01:10:43.340
let's say I'll take
the simpler one.

01:10:43.340 --> 01:10:45.697
And it turns out sometimes--
this is the lowest.

01:10:45.697 --> 01:10:46.530
This is the highest.

01:10:46.530 --> 01:10:48.330
It depends on-- this is a k.

01:10:48.330 --> 01:10:49.560
This is where I draw k.

01:10:49.560 --> 01:10:51.930
I'm drawing a small region.

01:10:51.930 --> 01:10:53.500
I can be drawing here.

01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:55.830
I can be drawing here.

01:10:55.830 --> 01:10:59.100
So, now this is my band gap.

01:10:59.100 --> 01:11:01.980
This is the EG, silicon EG.

01:11:01.980 --> 01:11:03.657
What is silicon EG?

01:11:03.657 --> 01:11:04.531
AUDIENCE: 0.1.

01:11:04.531 --> 01:11:08.510
PROFESSOR: 1.1,
1.12 electron volts.

01:11:08.510 --> 01:11:10.472
What's a gallium arsenide?

01:11:10.472 --> 01:11:12.664
AUDIENCE: 1.6.

01:11:12.664 --> 01:11:15.250
PROFESSOR: 1.4.

01:11:15.250 --> 01:11:22.010
So now I have some
thermal energy.

01:11:22.010 --> 01:11:26.770
So what happens is some
electron [INAUDIBLE] normally,

01:11:26.770 --> 01:11:29.260
will be locked from lower
energy to higher energy.

01:11:31.930 --> 01:11:35.380
So what it left behind
is some empty states.

01:11:35.380 --> 01:11:37.195
So now I have some empty states.

01:11:40.870 --> 01:11:44.710
And I have some filled states.

01:11:44.710 --> 01:11:46.630
And this is a conduction band.

01:11:46.630 --> 01:11:49.770
This is a valance band.

01:11:49.770 --> 01:11:52.140
Conduction band, valence band--

01:11:52.140 --> 01:11:56.020
valence band has
some empty states.

01:11:56.020 --> 01:11:59.440
And electrons are now
suddenly in this band.

01:11:59.440 --> 01:12:01.717
Again, because the energy
is so close to each other,

01:12:01.717 --> 01:12:03.050
those electrons can move around.

01:12:06.570 --> 01:12:08.940
And this electrons
fill to the top.

01:12:08.940 --> 01:12:13.910
Now, originally, if I had 0
temperature, they fill here.

01:12:13.910 --> 01:12:16.740
They can't move.

01:12:16.740 --> 01:12:19.360
But now [INAUDIBLE] some
temperature, room temperature--

01:12:19.360 --> 01:12:21.510
there's some empty
space left behind.

01:12:21.510 --> 01:12:26.950
So this electrons-- now they can
move around those empty states.

01:12:26.950 --> 01:12:29.060
Most of those electrons
here are sitting here.

01:12:29.060 --> 01:12:31.810
They don't move.

01:12:31.810 --> 01:12:36.760
So it's a one stone, two birds.

01:12:36.760 --> 01:12:39.280
The electron move
from here to here.

01:12:39.280 --> 01:12:41.710
The electron can move here.

01:12:41.710 --> 01:12:45.520
The empty states also make
the rest electron happier.

01:12:45.520 --> 01:12:49.030
When your lab is too crowded,
that's the situation, right?

01:12:49.030 --> 01:12:51.440
[CHUCKLES] The guys who
are moving to a bigger room

01:12:51.440 --> 01:12:51.940
are happy.

01:12:51.940 --> 01:12:53.680
And the guys left
behind, also happy.

01:12:53.680 --> 01:12:56.410
That's what happens to a lab.

01:12:56.410 --> 01:13:00.600
And so those empty states--

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:03.210
it's better than-- rather
than majority of the electron

01:13:03.210 --> 01:13:08.340
moving to empty states, the
opposite is there's holes.

01:13:08.340 --> 01:13:10.740
So it's a positive charge.

01:13:10.740 --> 01:13:13.240
So there's no hole.

01:13:13.240 --> 01:13:14.350
It's just a charge.

01:13:14.350 --> 01:13:19.670
It's easier to describe
these empty states as holes.

01:13:19.670 --> 01:13:21.830
And this is the electron.

01:13:21.830 --> 01:13:25.308
So we have valence band--

01:13:25.308 --> 01:13:26.709
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

01:13:26.709 --> 01:13:31.090
PROFESSOR: [SIGHS]
--conduction band--

01:13:31.090 --> 01:13:32.836
conduction band or valence band.

01:13:36.730 --> 01:13:37.795
And this is a valence.

01:13:45.890 --> 01:13:50.000
So you can say that
you have to really go

01:13:50.000 --> 01:13:52.370
to quantum to understand
even the basic-- why

01:13:52.370 --> 01:13:54.110
there is an insulator?

01:13:54.110 --> 01:13:56.565
Why there is a conductor?

01:13:56.565 --> 01:13:57.440
Why there is a metal?

01:14:00.390 --> 01:14:03.450
And now, I thought that--

01:14:03.450 --> 01:14:06.150
I'm debating whether
I show the slide

01:14:06.150 --> 01:14:10.470
or go to do our
weekly exercise--

01:14:10.470 --> 01:14:12.960
going to the website
or going to continue.

01:14:12.960 --> 01:14:14.430
But now let me-- just--

01:14:14.430 --> 01:14:16.290
because I think I
need to finish this.

01:14:16.290 --> 01:14:19.750
So I'm going to skip that.

01:14:19.750 --> 01:14:22.400
This is the intrinsic
semiconductor.

01:14:22.400 --> 01:14:25.890
There's always an equal
number of electron holes.

01:14:25.890 --> 01:14:27.320
Because if one
electron go up, it

01:14:27.320 --> 01:14:30.480
will leave behind a
hole, empty state.

01:14:30.480 --> 01:14:33.720
Now, most of the time you don't
work with just the intrinsic.

01:14:33.720 --> 01:14:38.300
You actually [INAUDIBLE]
So what do you do?

01:14:38.300 --> 01:14:40.540
You put in silicon--

01:14:40.540 --> 01:14:45.540
if you look at silicon,
it has 4 electrons.

01:14:45.540 --> 01:14:47.130
You put in phosphor--

01:14:47.130 --> 01:14:51.000
so silicon has a periodic
structure, 4 electron.

01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:52.710
They all happy.

01:14:52.710 --> 01:14:55.775
Now, rather than silicon,
you put the phosphor here.

01:14:55.775 --> 01:14:56.715
Now it's a 5.

01:14:59.320 --> 01:15:05.700
The actual electron can
detach from phosphor

01:15:05.700 --> 01:15:09.140
and become commonly shared.

01:15:09.140 --> 01:15:12.020
And so, basically, the
energy level of the phosphor

01:15:12.020 --> 01:15:12.910
is somewhere here.

01:15:12.910 --> 01:15:16.030
The thermal energy is
so hot-- is large enough

01:15:16.030 --> 01:15:19.660
to lift this electron from
phosphor to the conduction

01:15:19.660 --> 01:15:21.150
band.

01:15:21.150 --> 01:15:23.210
So, in that case, you
can put a-- you dope it.

01:15:23.210 --> 01:15:24.230
That's called doping.

01:15:24.230 --> 01:15:27.050
You artificially
put the dope in.

01:15:27.050 --> 01:15:28.100
You put the phosphor.

01:15:28.100 --> 01:15:29.450
That's an [INAUDIBLE].

01:15:29.450 --> 01:15:33.390
You put a boron,
which has 3 electron.

01:15:33.390 --> 01:15:38.100
What that does, though, it turns
out boron energy level is here.

01:15:38.100 --> 01:15:40.410
And then say the
electron is so happy

01:15:40.410 --> 01:15:43.050
to say a closed energy level.

01:15:43.050 --> 01:15:45.825
Once-- so you will fill here.

01:15:45.825 --> 01:15:50.490
You will say kT, so
leave behind empty state.

01:15:50.490 --> 01:15:51.690
So you have holes.

01:15:51.690 --> 01:15:53.370
So you dope.

01:15:53.370 --> 01:15:54.330
You borrow a dope.

01:15:54.330 --> 01:16:01.740
You get a [INAUDIBLE] You
double phosphor, you get n time.

01:16:01.740 --> 01:16:05.280
So that's the semiconductor.

01:16:05.280 --> 01:16:06.420
That's an extreme thing.

01:16:06.420 --> 01:16:09.720
So we have the difference
between extrinsic--

01:16:12.630 --> 01:16:13.890
that's a [INAUDIBLE].

01:16:13.890 --> 01:16:17.280
And the intrinsic is
when you don't dope it.

01:16:20.880 --> 01:16:25.530
And intrinsic, in fact--

01:16:25.530 --> 01:16:26.780
sometimes it's hard to make.

01:16:26.780 --> 01:16:31.880
When you purify silicon,
you can make that pure.

01:16:31.880 --> 01:16:36.350
And gallium arsenide, who have
semi-insulating substrate when

01:16:36.350 --> 01:16:40.160
you [INAUDIBLE],, that's because
[INAUDIBLE] band gap is 1.4,

01:16:40.160 --> 01:16:42.080
is higher than 1.1.

01:16:42.080 --> 01:16:47.615
And so there is a very few
electrons intrinsically

01:16:47.615 --> 01:16:49.490
if you try to purify
even though you'll still

01:16:49.490 --> 01:16:52.370
have some impurities.

01:16:52.370 --> 01:16:54.500
There's another big difference.

01:16:54.500 --> 01:16:57.620
Here, when I have--

01:16:57.620 --> 01:17:00.890
I draw here between
here and here,

01:17:00.890 --> 01:17:02.992
if the gap is happening
in different directions--

01:17:02.992 --> 01:17:04.700
you have to look at
different directions.

01:17:04.700 --> 01:17:07.700
I'm going to talk more
of this directionality.

01:17:07.700 --> 01:17:10.130
If this is not at
the same point--

01:17:10.130 --> 01:17:12.920
this is the momentum,
k momentum here.

01:17:12.920 --> 01:17:16.250
Electron-- hole momentum--
electron is here--

01:17:16.250 --> 01:17:20.550
goes there and need
a different momentum.

01:17:20.550 --> 01:17:22.180
There's a change.

01:17:22.180 --> 01:17:24.000
So that's an indirect
semiconductor.

01:17:24.000 --> 01:17:27.510
Silicon is an indirect
semiconductor.

01:17:27.510 --> 01:17:31.620
And in a lot of cases,
it turns out, also,

01:17:31.620 --> 01:17:34.800
the minimum and maximum
is the same place.

01:17:34.800 --> 01:17:37.170
That's a direct
gap semiconductor.

01:17:37.170 --> 01:17:40.330
Gallium arsenide
has a direct gap.

01:17:40.330 --> 01:17:44.440
So it turns out the light
doesn't have much momentum.

01:17:44.440 --> 01:17:46.840
If you think about them--

01:17:46.840 --> 01:17:51.280
h over lambda-- lambda
for light is 1/2 micron.

01:17:51.280 --> 01:17:53.350
For crystal, a is
a lattice constant.

01:17:53.350 --> 01:17:55.600
It's a [INAUDIBLE].

01:17:55.600 --> 01:17:59.020
So photon momentum
is very small.

01:17:59.020 --> 01:18:02.810
So when it's a direct
gap, you can easily

01:18:02.810 --> 01:18:05.800
excite because the momentum
conservation is easier because

01:18:05.800 --> 01:18:07.390
of vertical transmission.

01:18:07.390 --> 01:18:10.390
No momentum needed.

01:18:10.390 --> 01:18:13.320
But in silicon, that's
not easy because it's

01:18:13.320 --> 01:18:14.700
going from here to here.

01:18:14.700 --> 01:18:16.810
It needs that momentum.

01:18:16.810 --> 01:18:19.350
So it's an indirect
semiconductor.

01:18:19.350 --> 01:18:21.420
And that's why
the light source--

01:18:21.420 --> 01:18:24.120
lasers are made of
gallium arsenide.

01:18:24.120 --> 01:18:25.890
But always the
people want to say,

01:18:25.890 --> 01:18:27.600
can I make a light
source with silicon?

01:18:27.600 --> 01:18:29.670
Because silicon is so
good for electronics.

01:18:29.670 --> 01:18:32.460
It's not good for optics.

01:18:32.460 --> 01:18:36.150
And that's also a reason why--
silicon doesn't absorb well.

01:18:36.150 --> 01:18:37.830
So when you make
a solar cell, you

01:18:37.830 --> 01:18:39.720
have to make it
very [INAUDIBLE]..

01:18:39.720 --> 01:18:42.210
Because the chance
of light, again,

01:18:42.210 --> 01:18:45.880
when it gets into the crystal--
get absorbed is not good.

01:18:45.880 --> 01:18:48.420
So you make it thicker
to increase that chance.

01:18:51.365 --> 01:18:51.865
Yes?

01:18:51.865 --> 01:18:55.190
AUDIENCE: How do you decide
between [INAUDIBLE] hydrogen,

01:18:55.190 --> 01:18:55.880
for example?

01:18:55.880 --> 01:19:00.415
Where's the [INAUDIBLE]
when you [INAUDIBLE]??

01:19:00.415 --> 01:19:03.168
PROFESSOR: Hydrogen [INAUDIBLE]
my simple 1D picture--

01:19:03.168 --> 01:19:03.835
AUDIENCE: Right.

01:19:03.835 --> 01:19:05.710
PROFESSOR: --this is here.

01:19:05.710 --> 01:19:06.392
So it's a metal.

01:19:06.392 --> 01:19:08.350
I don't even call it the
valence of conduction.

01:19:08.350 --> 01:19:10.180
It's a metal.

01:19:10.180 --> 01:19:12.785
This is my conduction band.

01:19:12.785 --> 01:19:17.710
And helium here-- then if
I-- electron go from here,

01:19:17.710 --> 01:19:19.030
then this the valence.

01:19:19.030 --> 01:19:20.195
This is conduction.

01:19:20.195 --> 01:19:21.145
AUDIENCE: OK.

01:19:21.145 --> 01:19:24.550
So the highest [INAUDIBLE]

01:19:24.550 --> 01:19:27.200
PROFESSOR: Highest
occupied-- yeah, in fact,

01:19:27.200 --> 01:19:30.820
when you do molecule, this
is called Highest Occupied

01:19:30.820 --> 01:19:32.900
Molecular Orbital.

01:19:32.900 --> 01:19:35.470
So when you do, say,
plastic solar cells--

01:19:35.470 --> 01:19:37.750
so there are people talk
about HOMO and LUMO.

01:19:37.750 --> 01:19:41.680
Because the wave functions--
the wave vector is--

01:19:41.680 --> 01:19:43.690
the energy is no longer--

01:19:43.690 --> 01:19:44.710
this continues.

01:19:44.710 --> 01:19:47.695
It's a sort of discrete--

01:19:47.695 --> 01:19:50.980
your language,
actually, was official.

01:19:50.980 --> 01:19:54.770
CuMo and LUMO-- the Highest
Occupied-- the Highest Unoccu--

01:19:54.770 --> 01:19:57.340
Lowest Unoccupied.

01:19:57.340 --> 01:19:59.800
OK?

